<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">West Breifne</h1><p class="st-meta">1256 CE – 1605 CE (approx.) · capital Dromahair</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The O'Rourke lordship of Leitrim, heir to the old kingdom of Breifne, which lasted until the Elizabethan and Jacobean conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-breifne">Kingdom of Breifne</a> split in 1256, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-ruairc">O'Rourkes</a> held the western part, roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-leitrim">County Leitrim</a>, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-raghallaigh">O'Reillys</a> took the east. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dromahair">Dromahair</a>, by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-gill">Lough Gill</a>, became the O'Rourke seat.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>West Breifne was a land of small lakes, hills and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-raising, ruled through Gaelic law with bardic and learned families. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-ruairc">O'Rourkes</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/creevelea-friary">Creevelea Friary</a> in 1508. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-orourke">Brian O'Rourke</a> sheltered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> survivors in 1588 and was executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyburn">Tyburn</a> in 1591 for treason.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>His son Brian Og fought with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-oneill-earl-of-tyrone">O'Neill</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a>. After defeat the lordship was shired as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-leitrim">County Leitrim</a> and, in the early 17th century, planted with English settlers within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ireland">Kingdom of Ireland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/west-breifne.jpg" alt="West Breifne" width="320" height="400"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was (Automated conversion) at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland_1450.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1256 CE – 1605 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dromahair</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Brian O'Rourke, Brian Og O'Rourke</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Breifne O Rourke</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1430&amp;focus=west-breifne" aria-label="West Breifne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4497 318 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where West Breifne lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4817 574L4817 574M4817 574L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4817 574h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4817 574h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4817 574h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dromahair. <a href="/atlas?year=1430&amp;focus=west-breifne">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
